; expect: 11, 22, 33, 44
; An ELF object holds at most 16000 pieces. Past that count, neighbouring
; symbols share one piece, and a relocation names a private symbol by the
; section symbol of its piece plus the distance in the addend. A Global
; Offset Table load cannot use that addend: the linker adds it to the address
; of the table entry, and the load then reads the entry of another symbol.
; The globals below give the object more than 16000 symbols, so some probes
; are not at the start of their piece.

